          <span class="lesson-section-toggle">▾</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lesson-section-body">
          <div class="warning-box">
            <strong>⚠️ Never Mandate</strong>
            The Brain Break must always be presented as an <em>invitation</em>. Students who are not comfortable must be able to opt out. This is an individual choice.
          </div>
          <div class="warning-box">
            <strong>⚠️ Not a Compliance Tool</strong>
            Do NOT use the Brain Break as a classroom management strategy to enforce compliance. The goal is to help students develop internal self-regulation.
          </div>
          <div class="tip-box">
            <strong>✅ Right Mindset</strong>
            Focus on "practice" not "perfection." Minds will wander — that's normal! The goal is simply to notice wandering and gently return attention to the breath. Consistent practice matters more than doing it "right."
          </div>
        </div>
